g",4216,2811,{"large":56,"small":62,"medium":68,"thumbnail":73},{"ext":16,"url":57,"hash":58,"mime":19,"name":59,"path":7,"size":60,"width":22,"height":61},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/large_Post_08281_2_99a564c1d9.jpg","large_Post_08281_2_99a564c1d9","large_Post-08281-2.jpg",99.1,667,{"ext":16,"url":63,"hash":64,"mime":19,"name":65,"path":7,"size":66,"width":29,"height":67},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/small_Post_08281_2_99a564c1d9.jpg","small_Post_08281_2_99a564c1d9","small_Post-08281-2.jpg",31.68,333,{"ext":16,"url":69,"hash":70,"mime":19,"name":71,"path":7,"size":72,"width":36,"height":29},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/medium_Post_08281_2_99a564c1d9.jpg","medium_Post_08281_2_99a564c1d9","medium_Post-08281-2.jpg",61.07,{"ext":16,"url":74,"hash":75,"mime":19,"name":76,"path":7,"size":77,"width":78,"height":79},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/thumbnail_Post_08281_2_99a564c1d9.jpg","thumbnail_Post_08281_2_99a564c1d9","thumbnail_Post-08281-2.jpg",9.2,234,156,1344.91,"Post-08281-2.jpg","2025-10-26T09:24:08.516Z",{"id":84,"url":85,"alternativeText":7,"caption":7,"width":86,"height":87,"formats":88,"mime":19,"size":109,"name":110,"provider":47,"createdAt":111,"updatedAt":111},35,"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/Post_08311_0ca6bd2428.jpg",4143,2762,{"large":89,"small":94,"medium":99,"thumbnail":104},{"ext":16,"url":90,"hash":91,"mime":19,"name":92,"path":7,"size":93,"width":22,"height":61},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/large_Post_08311_0ca6bd2428.jpg","large_Post_08311_0ca6bd2428","large_Post-08311.jpg",109.75,{"ext":16,"url":95,"hash":96,"mime":19,"name":97,"path":7,"size":98,"width":29,"height":67},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/small_Post_08311_0ca6bd2428.jpg","small_Post_08311_0ca6bd2428","small_Post-08311.jpg",35.6,{"ext":16,"url":100,"hash":101,"mime":19,"name":102,"path":7,"size":103,"width":36,"height":29},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/medium_Post_08311_0ca6bd2428.jpg","medium_Post_08311_0ca6bd2428","medium_Post-08311.jpg",67.48,{"ext":16,"url":105,"hash":106,"mime":19,"name":107,"path":7,"size":108,"width":78,"height":79},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/thumbnail_Post_08311_0ca6bd2428.jpg","thumbnail_Post_08311_0ca6bd2428","thumbnail_Post-08311.jpg",10.45,1601.19,"Post-08311.jpg","2025-10-26T09:24:08.618Z",{"id":113,"url":114,"alternativeText":7,"caption":7,"width":115,"height":116,"formats":117,"mime":19,"size":138,"name":139,"provider":47,"createdAt":140,"updatedAt":140},36,"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/Post_08331_8589f9f741.jpg",6000,4000,{"large":118,"small":123,"medium":128,"thumbnail":133},{"ext":16,"url":119,"hash":120,"mime":19,"name":121,"path":7,"size":122,"width":22,"height":61},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/large_Post_08331_8589f9f741.jpg","large_Post_08331_8589f9f741","large_Post-08331.jpg",93.81,{"ext":16,"url":124,"hash":125,"mime":19,"name":126,"path":7,"size":127,"width":29,"height":67},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/small_Post_08331_8589f9f741.jpg","small_Post_08331_8589f9f741","small_Post-08331.jpg",32.14,{"ext":16,"url":129,"hash":130,"mime":19,"name":131,"path":7,"size":132,"width":36,"height":29},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/medium_Post_08331_8589f9f741.jpg","medium_Post_08331_8589f9f741","medium_Post-08331.jpg",61.01,{"ext":16,"url":134,"hash":135,"mime":19,"name":136,"path":7,"size":137,"width":78,"height":79},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/thumbnail_Post_08331_8589f9f741.jpg","thumbnail_Post_08331_8589f9f741","thumbnail_Post-08331.jpg",9.78,2071.39,"Post-08331.jpg","2025-10-26T09:24:10.555Z","On 27 July 2025, the COLOCAL project under the Department of Environmental Science and Management organised a Policy Dialogue session at the CARITAS Regional Office in Barisal. This was done in partnership with the Locally Led Adaptation (LLA) Programme at the International Center for Climate Change and Development for their launch of an LLA divisional platform in Barisal.\n\nTwo students from the 2025 COLOCAL Fellowship cohort, Ragib Mahmood Shuvo and Syed Irfan Uddin,  presented their research proposals to local GO/NGO representatives, academicians, youth leaders, and others participating at the event. The session was facilitated by Fahmid Mohtasin, Project Officer for COLOCAL.\n\nThinking of the ecosystem as a living entity, Syed Irfan Uddin’s research idea focused on how cyclones impact the surrounding regions and how the local community can take anticipatory actions to reduce, restore, and revive the essential services the ecosystem provides. A mixed-methodology approach, incorporating Machine Learning models and a community survey, would be used to identify the most vulnerable ecosystems by considering the extent of community reliance on them. Participants in the policy dialogue provided valuable feedback on integrating policy and utilising the assessment and prediction tool to better support the community in developing locally led adaptation strategies.\n\nRagib Mahmood Shuvo presented his proposed MSc thesis as well, which aims to investigate groundwater salinity intrusion in coastal Bangladesh to inform locally-led adaptation. The study integrates three key methods: geospatial modeling to map salinity pathways, future risk scenario analysis to project climate impacts, and a community-based assessment to understand local adaptive capacities. This comprehensive approach aims to provide actionable insights for developing sustainable and community-supported solutions. The presentation sparked thoughtful feedback from the local stakeholders, who emphasised the need for preventative groundwater protection and technology-driven yet locally supported solutions.\n\n_The COLOCAL project is under the NORHED programme of NORAD with IUB as an implementing partner._\n\nPhotos: Md Shahadat H Shahal\n\n***Media Coverage***\nhttps://iub.ac.bd/news-and-events/news-archive/2025-July/68ae76a92694aff82408a07d\n",false,{"id":144,"title":145,"secondaryTitle":7,"date":146,"cover":147,"images":174,"body":247,"section":7,"lla":142,"projects":7},18,"IUB Delegates Represent COLOCAL Project at the Adaptation Futures 2025 Conference in New Zealand","2025-10-26",{"id":148,"url":149,"alternativeText":7,"caption":7,"width":150,"height":151,"formats":152,"mime":19,"size":171,"name":172,"provider":47,"createdAt":173,"updatedAt":173},37,"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/IMG_20251022_WA_0129_fbe64837e3.jpg",872,654,{"small":153,"medium":159,"thumbnail":165},{"ext":16,"url":154,"hash":155,"mime":19,"name":156,"path":7,"size":157,"width":29,"height":158},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/small_IMG_20251022_WA_0129_fbe64837e3.jpg","small_IMG_20251022_WA_0129_fbe64837e3","small_IMG-20251022-WA0129.jpg",30.37,375,{"ext":16,"url":160,"hash":161,"mime":19,"name":162,"path":7,"size":163,"width":36,"height":164},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/medium_IMG_20251022_WA_0129_fbe64837e3.jpg","medium_IMG_20251022_WA_0129_fbe64837e3","medium_IMG-20251022-WA0129.jpg",56.49,563,{"ext":16,"url":166,"hash":167,"mime":19,"name":168,"path":7,"size":169,"width":170,"height":79},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/thumbnail_IMG_20251022_WA_0129_fbe64837e3.jpg","thumbnail_IMG_20251022_WA_0129_fbe64837e3","thumbnail_IMG-20251022-WA0129.jpg",7.5,208,68.34,"IMG-20251022-WA0129.jpg","2025-10-27T04:34:42.022Z",[175,199,223],{"id":176,"url":177,"alternativeText":7,"caption":7,"width":178,"height":179,"formats":180,"mime":19,"size":196,"name":197,"provider":47,"createdAt":198,"updatedAt":198},38,"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/IMG_20251022_WA_0122_04007c84a5.jpg",816,612,{"small":181,"medium":186,"thumbnail":191},{"ext":16,"url":182,"hash":183,"mime":19,"name":184,"path":7,"size":185,"width":29,"height":158},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/small_IMG_20251022_WA_0122_04007c84a5.jpg","small_IMG_20251022_WA_0122_04007c84a5","small_IMG-20251022-WA0122.jpg",32.31,{"ext":16,"url":187,"hash":188,"mime":19,"name":189,"path":7,"size":190,"width":36,"height":164},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/medium_IMG_20251022_WA_0122_04007c84a5.jpg","medium_IMG_20251022_WA_0122_04007c84a5","medium_IMG-20251022-WA0122.jpg",60.97,{"ext":16,"url":192,"hash":193,"mime":19,"name":194,"path":7,"size":195,"width":170,"height":79},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/thumbnail_IMG_20251022_WA_0122_04007c84a5.jpg","thumbnail_IMG_20251022_WA_0122_04007c84a5","thumbnail_IMG-20251022-WA0122.jpg",7.72,66.92,"IMG-20251022-WA0122.jpg","2025-10-27T04:35:09.808Z",{"id":200,"url":201,"alternativeText":7,"caption":7,"width":202,"height":203,"formats":204,"mime":19,"size":220,"name":221,"provider":47,"createdAt":222,"updatedAt":222},39,"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/IMG_20251022_WA_0125_5c534867cb.jpg",948,711,{"small":205,"medium":210,"thumbnail":215},{"ext":16,"url":206,"hash":207,"mime":19,"name":208,"path":7,"size":209,"width":29,"height":158},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/small_IMG_20251022_WA_0125_5c534867cb.jpg","small_IMG_20251022_WA_0125_5c534867cb","small_IMG-20251022-WA0125.jpg",33.47,{"ext":16,"url":211,"hash":212,"mime":19,"name":213,"path":7,"size":214,"width":36,"height":164},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/medium_IMG_20251022_WA_0125_5c534867cb.jpg","medium_IMG_20251022_WA_0125_5c534867cb","medium_IMG-20251022-WA0125.jpg",62.7,{"ext":16,"url":216,"hash":217,"mime":19,"name":218,"path":7,"size":219,"width":170,"height":79},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/thumbnail_IMG_20251022_WA_0125_5c534867cb.jpg","thumbnail_IMG_20251022_WA_0125_5c534867cb","thumbnail_IMG-20251022-WA0125.jpg",8.21,80.4,"IMG-20251022-WA0125.jpg","2025-10-27T04:35:10.004Z",{"id":224,"url":225,"alternativeText":7,"caption":7,"width":226,"height":227,"formats":228,"mime":19,"size":244,"name":245,"provider":47,"createdAt":246,"updatedAt":246},40,"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/IMG_20251022_WA_0128_7ee898dcfd.jpg",916,687,{"small":229,"medium":234,"thumbnail":239},{"ext":16,"url":230,"hash":231,"mime":19,"name":232,"path":7,"size":233,"width":29,"height":158},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/small_IMG_20251022_WA_0128_7ee898dcfd.jpg","small_IMG_20251022_WA_0128_7ee898dcfd","small_IMG-20251022-WA0128.jpg",25.63,{"ext":16,"url":235,"hash":236,"mime":19,"name":237,"path":7,"size":238,"width":36,"height":164},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/medium_IMG_20251022_WA_0128_7ee898dcfd.jpg","medium_IMG_20251022_WA_0128_7ee898dcfd","medium_IMG-20251022-WA0128.jpg",48.44,{"ext":16,"url":240,"hash":241,"mime":19,"name":242,"path":7,"size":243,"width":170,"height":79},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/thumbnail_IMG_20251022_WA_0128_7ee898dcfd.jpg","thumbnail_IMG_20251022_WA_0128_7ee898dcfd","thumbnail_IMG-20251022-WA0128.jpg",6.78,58.68,"IMG-20251022-WA0128.jpg","2025-10-27T04:35:10.294Z","Delegates from Independent University, Bangladesh (IUB) took part in the Adaptation Futures 2025 Conference, held in Christchurch, New Zealand, from October 13 to 16, 2025. The participation was under the Norad-funded COLOCAL (Co-creating Knowledge for Locally Led Climate Change Adaptation) project, which focuses on advancing locally led adaptation through collaborative research and partnerships across the Global South and North.\n\nRepresenting IUB were Dr. K. Ayaz Rabbani, Associate Professor and Project Coordinator of COLOCAL, and Fahmid Mohtasin, Research Officer for the project. They joined COLOCAL collaborators from the Norwegian University of Life Sciences (NMBU), including Professor Matthew Cashmore, Project Lead of COLOCAL, and Professor Siri Eriksen, for a panel discussion titled “Making Locally Led Adaptation a Reality: Advances from Research on and with Indigenous and Local Peoples.”\n\nThe panel, held on October 15 from 11:30 AM to 12:45 PM, brought together researchers working on the frontlines of climate adaptation with indigenous and local communities. Discussions centered on the practical challenges and opportunities of implementing locally led adaptation and the importance of co-producing knowledge that reflects community realities.\n\nThe session also featured online contributions from Ishrat Jahan, a COLOCAL Fellow from the 2022 cohort at IUB, Graca Jonas, a PhD student at Eduardo Mondlane University (Mozambique), and Edwige Marty, a PhD student at NMBU (Norway). Their participation enriched the dialogue with insights from different regional contexts, emphasizing COLOCAL’s truly collaborative and cross-regional approach.\n\nThe Adaptation Futures 2025 Conference is one of the world’s leading events on climate adaptation and brings together global experts, practitioners, and policymakers to share innovative research and practical experiences. IUB’s involvement reflects its ongoing commitment to advancing climate adaptation research and contributing to global discussions on resilience, local leadership, and sustainable development.\n\nFor more information about the COLOCAL project, visit: [https://www.luccc.org/projects/colocal](link)",{"id":249,"title":250,"secondaryTitle":7,"date":251,"cover":252,"images":7,"body":282,"section":7,"lla":142,"projects":7},11,"COLOCAL Fellows of Bangladesh Present Research at COLOCAL Seminar Series","2025-07-28",{"id":253,"url":254,"alternativeText":7,"caption":7,"width":255,"height":255,"formats":256,"mime":261,"size":279,"name":280,"provider":47,"createdAt":281,"updatedAt":281},15,"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/Blue_And_White_Modern_Marketing_Seminar_Instagram_Post_691382207b.png",1080,{"large":257,"small":264,"medium":269,"thumbnail":274},{"ext":258,"url":259,"hash":260,"mime":261,"name":262,"path":7,"size":263,"width":22,"height":22},".png","https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/large_Blue_And_White_Modern_Marketing_Seminar_Instagram_Post_691382207b.png","large_Blue_And_White_Modern_Marketing_Seminar_Instagram_Post_691382207b","image/png","large_Blue And White Modern Marketing Seminar Instagram Post.png",1374.45,{"ext":258,"url":265,"hash":266,"mime":261,"name":267,"path":7,"size":268,"width":29,"height":29},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/small_Blue_And_White_Modern_Marketing_Seminar_Instagram_Post_691382207b.png","small_Blue_And_White_Modern_Marketing_Seminar_Instagram_Post_691382207b","small_Blue And White Modern Marketing Seminar Instagram Post.png",392.77,{"ext":258,"url":270,"hash":271,"mime":261,"name":272,"path":7,"size":273,"width":36,"height":36},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/medium_Blue_And_White_Modern_Marketing_Seminar_Instagram_Post_691382207b.png","medium_Blue_And_White_Modern_Marketing_Seminar_Instagram_Post_691382207b","medium_Blue And White Modern Marketing Seminar Instagram Post.png",825.98,{"ext":258,"url":275,"hash":276,"mime":261,"name":277,"path":7,"size":278,"width":79,"height":79},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/thumbnail_Blue_And_White_Modern_Marketing_Seminar_Instagram_Post_691382207b.png","thumbnail_Blue_And_White_Modern_Marketing_Seminar_Instagram_Post_691382207b","thumbnail_Blue And White Modern Marketing Seminar Instagram Post.png",54.43,310.27,"Blue And White Modern Marketing Seminar Instagram Post.png","2025-10-07T12:03:44.443Z","Bangladesh hosted the July session of the COLOCAL Seminar Series after Mozambique led the first event in June. The monthly seminar was started at the COLOCAL annual meeting in Uganda to help fellows from different countries learn from each other and share their work. The July session featured three fellows from Independent University, Bangladesh (IUB) - Mohammad Julfiqar Haider, Rafia Anjum Rimi, and Chowdhury Alfi Afroze. Their research showed Bangladesh’s strong role in promoting locally led adaptation (LLA) and climate resilience.\n\nMohammad Julfiqar Haider presented his study, “Exploring Effective Strategies for Integrating Locally Led Adaptation (LLA) into NGOs in Bangladesh.” His research focused on Shyamnagar, a coastal area that faces many climate risks. He talked with NGOs such as BRAC, LEDARS, and UNDP to understand how they use LLA in their projects. His findings showed that many organizations involve communities in planning but face several problems such as strict donor rules, limited local capacity, and lack of national policy support. He suggested more flexible funding, better policy alignment, and stronger cooperation among NGOs, government, and donors.\n\nRafia Anjum Rimi presented her thesis proposal, “From Community-Based to Locally Led Adaptation: Assessing Effectiveness for Climate Migrants in Khulna’s Urban Informal Settlements.” She is studying how different types of local leadership such as ward-level, municipal, or settlement-based  affect adaptation results. She explained that climate migrants often face land insecurity and are excluded from city planning. Her study will recommend ways to make local governance more inclusive and secure for these vulnerable groups.\n\nChowdhury Alfi Afroze shared her research titled “Reimagining Coastal Resilience: Indigenous Adaptation, Nature-Based Solutions and Biotech for Sustainable Farming in Bangladesh.” She aims to link traditional farming knowledge with modern biotechnology and nature-based methods. Afroze found that scientific innovations are often not accessible to rural farmers. Her research suggests combining indigenous knowledge, sustainable agriculture, and biotech tools to build climate-smart and resilient farming systems.\nThe seminar ended with positive feedback from faculty and fellows. The session reflected COLOCAL’s goal to connect young researchers and support local solutions for climate change across partner countries.\n",{"id":284,"title":285,"secondaryTitle":7,"date":286,"cover":287,"images":314,"body":396,"section":7,"lla":142,"projects":7},19,"COLOCAL Project holds Policy Dialogue on Climate Change Adaptation in Khulna, Bangladesh","2024-11-07",{"id":288,"url":289,"alternativeText":7,"caption":7,"width":115,"height":116,"formats":290,"mime":19,"size":311,"name":312,"provider":47,"createdAt":313,"updatedAt":313},9,"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/1_481d76f79f.jpg",{"large":291,"small":296,"medium":301,"thumbnail":306},{"ext":16,"url":292,"hash":293,"mime":19,"name":294,"path":7,"size":295,"width":22,"height":61},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/large_1_481d76f79f.jpg","large_1_481d76f79f","large_1.jpg",88.42,{"ext":16,"url":297,"hash":298,"mime":19,"name":299,"path":7,"size":300,"width":29,"height":67},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/small_1_481d76f79f.jpg","small_1_481d76f79f","small_1.jpg",29.29,{"ext":16,"url":302,"hash":303,"mime":19,"name":304,"path":7,"size":305,"width":36,"height":29},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/medium_1_481d76f79f.jpg","medium_1_481d76f79f","medium_1.jpg",56.46,{"ext":16,"url":307,"hash":308,"mime":19,"name":309,"path":7,"size":310,"width":78,"height":79},"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/thumbnail_1_481d76f79f.jpg","thumbnail_1_481d76f79f","thumbnail_1.jpg",9.05,1257.09,"1.jpg","2025-10-02T16:58:13.783Z",[315,342,369],{"id":316,"url":317,"alternativeText":7,"caption":7,"width":115,"height":116,"formats":318,"mime":19,"size":339,"name":340,"provider":47,"createdAt":341,"updatedAt":341},59,"https://genuine-baseball-c50454a875.media.strapiapp.com/KPD_1_29_18bee1df2c.jpg",{"large":319,"small":324,"medium":329,"thumbnail":334},{"ext":16,"url":320,